+## APPENDED CORRECTION — 2026-09-09 (EXPR-COMPOSITION-2)
+
+The text above is preserved verbatim. Three statements in it are corrected here.
+
+**1 · §3 and §4 are wrong about marker completeness.** §3 says the 22 markers are "readable on
+**both** platforms for **all** 35 GPL6244 and 16 GPL3290 labelled samples", repeating
+`PREREGISTRATION.md` §2. That is true on GPL6244 and **false on GPL3290**, where per-sample
+`z_vs_array` is missing for DCN (8 of 16 samples), CD3E (4), MS4A1 (3), PTPRC (2), and CD8A,
+HLA-DRA and MKI67 (1 each). Because `C` is a NaN-skipping mean, `C` on GPL3290 is a mean over a
+**sample-dependent 16–20 marker set** whose count correlates **+0.2105** with the EMC label — not
+the single fixed score §4 describes. See `PREREGISTRATION.md`, appended correction C1.
+
+**2 · The headline attenuation depends on that defect.** Recomputing the whole analysis with a
+**fixed 14-marker score** (the markers complete on every labelled sample of both platforms; no
+NaN-skipping) gives, on the same frames and machinery:
+
+| frame | unadjusted | adjusted, fixed 14-marker score | attenuation of the excess over 0.5 | published figure |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| primary | 0.6521 | **0.6129** | **0.2576** | 0.561 |
+| secondary | 0.6368 | **0.6199** | **0.1239** | 0.283 |
+
+Against 2000 label permutations with the adjustment in place the residual is **stronger**, not
+weaker, than reported: p = 0.0010 (primary) and 0.0015 (secondary). Further, matched sham
+covariates show the fixed-score attenuation is **not** distinguishable from the generic shrinkage
+any label-correlated covariate produces (4/14, 14/39 and 30/76 matched shams attenuate at least as
+much; one-sided p = 0.33–0.40). §5's "roughly half of the excess concordance", §6's "0.561 is an
+upper bound on the composition share", and §7's "roughly half … and about 28 %" should therefore
+not be quoted. Derivation and limits: `../EXPR-COMPOSITION-2/FINDING.md` and its `checks/`.
+
+**3 · A frozen parameter was changed without disclosure.** `PREREGISTRATION.md` §3 froze
+`N_PERM_COMP = 2000` composition permutations for the negative control; the published run used
+**500** (`N_PERM_COMP_NC = 500`). §5 reports the 500 but never as a departure from the freeze. It
+is one, and is recorded as one here and in the preregistration's appended correction C2.
